# Amy voice ownership (mandatory)

TTS playback is owned by `amy-voice-controller.ts`. UI must never bypass it.

## Allowed (UI / components)

- `useAmyVoice().speak(text, opts?)` — start playback
- `useAmyVoice().pause()` — explicit user intent only (close, back, toggle off)
- `useAmyVoice().primeSpeakGesture()` — Android gesture priming on pointerdown

## Forbidden

- `useAmyVoice().stop()` — removed; use `pause()`
- `useEffect(() => () => pause(), [])` or any lifecycle cleanup that stops audio
- Direct `audioManager.stop()` / `stopAll()` outside controller/pipeline
- Importing `@/lib/amy-voice-ownership` from UI code

## Enforcement

- CI: `pnpm check:amy-voice` (usage + contract scripts + unit tests)
- Dev: controller warns when `audioManager.stop*` is called outside controlled paths

## When closing modals / sheets

Call `pause()` in the close handler, not in unmount effects:

```tsx
const handleClose = () => {
  pause();
  onClose();
};
```
